  "body": "## Cause\n\nPR #3485 (#3447) changed the setup order of the program from the name order to the creation order. This change is on purpose. The MCP test `move_an_operation_delete_the_emptied_setup_and_undo_redo_both` in `crates/app/tests/mcp_setup_moves.rs` still asserted the old name order after the undo of `delete_setup`. The test creates \"Front\" first and \"Back\" second, so the correct order is `[\"Front\",\"Back\"]`. The post-merge run 45093122162 on edcbfe4dd failed on this assert.\n\nThe product is correct. `setup_delete_order` (added by #3485) pins the product undo: undo of `DeleteSetup` puts the setup back at its old place, and the posted program does not change.\n\n## Change (test only)\n\n- Old: after `undo`, `assert_eq!(c.shape().0, vec![\"Back\", \"Front\"])` (name order).\n- New: before the delete, the test captures the setup list and asserts `[\"Front\",\"Back\"]` (creation order). After `undo`, it asserts that the list is equal to the captured list.\n- New: after `redo` and the next `undo`, the test asserts the captured list again. The old test did not assert the list at this point.\n\nNo undo or redo assert is weaker. No product code changes. No post output changes. `PROJECT_VERSION` stays 77.\n\n## Readings and pinning tests\n\nAll runs are debug, `-j 6`, by binary name, on head 1c6002baa:\n\n- `mcp_setup_moves`: 3 passed (the failing test is green).\n- Each `crates/app/tests/mcp*.rs` binary (49 binaries, `mcp` to `mcp_workholding`): all pass, 0 failed.\n- `setup_creation_order`: 4 passed. `setup_delete_order`: 2 passed. `setups`: 12 passed. `project_roundtrip`: 80 passed.\n- `camcraft-app --lib`: 298 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --lib -- -D warnings`: clean. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test mcp_setup_moves -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not run\n\n- The other app test binaries, the UI suites, the light lane and the heavy lanes. The diff changes one test file only.\n\nEffort: high (the issue label is effort:low; the coordinator sent it to the high tier).\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #3602\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
